Fame\nEHA Travel Grants\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\nScope of our grants\nPrecision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\nTuesday, May 6, 2025\nEHA Mentorship Program\nMenu\nClose\nConnect & Network\nEHA2027 Congress\nEHA2027 registration\nEHA2027 program\nEHA2027 abstract submission\nEHA2027 travel grants & abstract awards\nEHA2027 sponsorship opportunities\nEHA2027 details and deadlines\nEHA2027 sustainability\nEHA2026 Congress\nEHA2026 Congress platform\nEHA2026 sustainability\nCongress archive\nEHA2026 Perspectives Congress Report\nEHA2026 gallery\nEHA2025 Perspectives Congress Reports\nEHA2025 gallery\nEHA2024 Chair's wrap-up\nEHA2024 report\nEHA2024 gallery\nEHA2023 report\nEHA2023 gallery\nScientific meetings\nMembership\nFull membership\nJunior membership\nTrial membership\nHealthcare-affiliated professional membership\nEmeritus membership\nJoint EHA and national society membership\nUsing MyEHA\nClinical practice\nOur guidelines initiative\nGuidelines by areas of disease\nEHA Guidelines app\nEHA Clinical Guidelines Webinar Series\nBedside Hematology – Rapid Reference\nEducation & Training\nEHA Campus\nLearning paths\nEuropean Hematology Curriculum\nEntrustable Professional Activities\nLighting the Flame Program\nTests and tools\nEHA Diagnosis\nEHA Exam\nProgress Test\nMentoring and career development\nCareer comparison tool\nEHA Mentorship Program\nMaster Class\nResearch training programs\nEHA-EMBO Lab Leadership Course\nResearch & Innovation\nHemaSphere\nSpecialized Working Groups\nSupport for SWG scientific meetings\nSWG Grants\nHow to apply to join an SWG\nWebinars and online groups\nSWG Preceptorship Program\nGrants\nEHA Research Grants\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\nEHA Innovation Grant\nEHA Kick-off Grant\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\nEHA Travel Grants\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\nScope of our grants\nTopics-in-Focus program\nPrecision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\nCongress\nHemaSphere\nAbout EHA\nSearch\nJoin EHA\nLogin\nSpecialized Working Groups\nHome\nResearch & Innovation\nSpecialized Working Groups\nEHA’s Specialized Working Groups (SWGs) foster science and spread knowledge in basic, translational, and clinical research in hematology.\nTo ensure we cover the full field of hematology and provide a research platform for all groups and researchers, we’ve established two types of SWG:\nDisease-oriented SWGs—which cover specific topics such as leukemias and lymphomas\nOverarching SWGs—which cover broad themes such as aging and precision medicine\nThis model is based on the nine sections of the EHA Roadmap for European Hematology Research.\nThere are currently 25 SWGs. You can use the filter below to view them by type.\nHow to join an SWG\nIf you’re interested in making new connections or sharing your expertise, you can apply to join an SWG. To do this, just follow the instructions on the main page of the relevant SWG.\nSWG Grants\nEHA provides financial support to small research projects initiated by our SWGs. You can find out more about his support, and discover some of the projects we’ve already supported, in the SWG Grants section.\nEHA Lymphoma Group\nEuropean Research Initiative on CLL (ERIC)\nEuropean Scientific foundation for Laboratory Hemato Oncology (ESLHO)\nOverarching Specialized Working Group on Diagnostics in Hematology\nSpecialized Working Group on Acute Myeloid Leukemia\nSpecialized Working Group on Adolescents and Young Adults with Hematologic Diseases (AYA)\nSpecialized Working Group on Adult Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia\nSpecialized Working Group on Aging and Hematology\nSpecialized Working Group on Bleeding and Thrombosis\nSpecialized Working Group on Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML)\nSpecialized Working Group on Diagnosis in Hematological Diseases: Morphology and Flow Cytometry\nSpecialized Working Group on Genetic Predisposition to Blood Cancer (Rare Diseases)\nJoin 